WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.763
Welcome.

2
00:00:00.763 --> 00:00:04.247
This is the narrated briefing
for a companion guide in the

3
00:00:04.247 --> 00:00:08.312
Federal Modernization Workbook:
The Daily Checks on One Dashboard.

4
00:00:08.312 --> 00:00:11.987
One thing first: the guide has
been reviewed and approved.

5
00:00:11.987 --> 00:00:15.433
It answers a question the
operator runbook leaves open:

6
00:00:15.433 --> 00:00:19.701
can the operator see all of the daily
checks in one place each morning?

7
00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:24.109
Mostly yes, on one Azure Monitor workbook
in the Sentinel workspace, with a

8
00:00:24.109 --> 00:00:28.663
link out to the portal that holds the data
for the checks a workbook can't read.

9
00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:34.088
Its facts come from Microsoft Learn,
read on November eighteenth, 2026.

10
00:00:34.088 --> 00:00:37.960
We'll go in four parts:
why, what, who, and how.

11
00:00:41.710 --> 00:00:43.635
Here's the rule the guide keeps.

12
00:00:43.635 --> 00:00:48.211
The Security Operations book says it
plainly: a dashboard is a picture of the

13
00:00:48.211 --> 00:00:50.535
evidence; what an assessor relies on is

14
00:00:50.535 --> 00:00:53.585
regenerating the numbers
from the stored records.

15
00:00:53.585 --> 00:00:56.821
The Compliance Automation
book says the same of tests:

16
00:00:56.821 --> 00:01:00.560
one that reads a dashboard tile
is a screenshot with a schedule.

17
00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:03.073
So the workbook in this guide is a view.

18
00:01:03.073 --> 00:01:08.536
Every tab says so, and the kit refuses
to record a rendered view as evidence.

19
00:01:08.536 --> 00:01:11.341
The evidence stays where it already lives:

20
00:01:11.341 --> 00:01:15.870
in the record each check writes,
and the task each finding opens.

21
00:01:19.620 --> 00:01:20.945
What does Azure offer?

22
00:01:20.945 --> 00:01:23.570
Microsoft's guidance compares the options.

23
00:01:23.570 --> 00:01:28.520
Workbooks are a flexible canvas over the
most complete set of Azure data sources,

24
00:01:28.520 --> 00:01:31.845
and they can be managed as
Resource Manager templates.

25
00:01:31.845 --> 00:01:36.433
Portal dashboards give a single pane
of glass, but a workbook is richer.

26
00:01:36.433 --> 00:01:41.300
Dashboards with Grafana is a free
preview; Azure Managed Grafana is for

27
00:01:41.300 --> 00:01:46.333
external sources and private networking;
Power BI suits long-term trends.

28
00:01:46.333 --> 00:01:49.811
Microsoft 365 has no
single custom dashboard:

29
00:01:49.811 --> 00:01:53.107
each admin center has
its own built-in views.

30
00:01:53.107 --> 00:01:56.191
So the design is one workbook
in the Sentinel workspace,

31
00:01:56.191 --> 00:01:59.040
and a link out where the
data stays elsewhere.

32
00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:05.615
Here are the ten tabs,
one per daily check.

33
00:02:05.615 --> 00:02:09.129
Telemetry completeness,
the synchronization probe,

34
00:02:09.129 --> 00:02:13.602
risky users and sign-ins, and
emergency access sign-ins fit strongly.

35
00:02:13.602 --> 00:02:17.403
Noncompliant devices and
D L P alerts fit well.

36
00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:21.903
Grants and the log review queue are
partial: the grants tab lists them,

37
00:02:21.903 --> 00:02:25.220
but matching each to a ticket
stays in the I T S M tool,

38
00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:30.590
and the log review tab shows the queue
while the review stays a recorded procedure.

39
00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:35.040
Entra Health is a link-out, because
its alerts aren't in Log Analytics.

40
00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:40.460
And the catalog tasks live in the
I T S M tool's own dashboards.

41
00:02:44.210 --> 00:02:46.398
What's available in G C C?

42
00:02:46.398 --> 00:02:52.044
G C C Moderate uses the commercial Entra
service and pairs with commercial Azure, so

43
00:02:52.044 --> 00:02:57.610
the workspace, the workbook and the Logs
Ingestion API are all in commercial Azure.

44
00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:00.435
Sentinel workbooks are
generally available there.

45
00:03:00.435 --> 00:03:04.315
Entra and Intune both send
their logs to the workspace;

46
00:03:04.315 --> 00:03:09.747
Microsoft says Intune in G C C is the
same instance as the commercial service.

47
00:03:09.747 --> 00:03:14.922
Defender X D R alerts and incidents
are generally available for G C C.

48
00:03:14.922 --> 00:03:17.633
The Defender portal's
connector overview is a

49
00:03:17.633 --> 00:03:20.272
commercial-cloud preview,
so it isn't assumed.

50
00:03:20.272 --> 00:03:24.431
And Entra Health monitoring and
Connect Health are not yet specified,

51
00:03:24.431 --> 00:03:26.360
so their tabs are link-outs.

52
00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.035
Who does what?

53
00:03:31.035 --> 00:03:34.025
Security operations is
accountable for the sources,

54
00:03:34.025 --> 00:03:38.035
the template and the deployment, and
for the telemetry tab each morning.

55
00:03:38.035 --> 00:03:42.020
Identity engineering connects
the Entra logs and the probe,

56
00:03:42.020 --> 00:03:45.048
and supplies the emergency
access object I D's.

57
00:03:45.048 --> 00:03:50.210
The endpoint platform owner connects Intune
and supplies the compliance state value.

58
00:03:50.210 --> 00:03:53.098
The operators read
their own family's tabs.

59
00:03:53.098 --> 00:03:56.128
And the security officer
is consulted on each plan,

60
00:03:56.128 --> 00:04:01.030
approving its hash in the change record,
and is accountable for the evidence.

61
00:04:04.780 --> 00:04:06.092
Now the six steps.

62
00:04:06.092 --> 00:04:08.305
Step 1 connects the sources.

63
00:04:08.305 --> 00:04:13.568
An Entra diagnostic setting sends sign-in,
audit and risk logs to the workspace.

64
00:04:13.568 --> 00:04:17.403
Intune's diagnostic settings
send the compliance export,

65
00:04:17.403 --> 00:04:19.880
once a day, up to forty-eight hours late.

66
00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:23.521
The Defender X D R connector
brings incidents and alerts,

67
00:04:23.521 --> 00:04:26.464
including those it collects
from Purview D L P.

68
00:04:26.464 --> 00:04:29.330
Health monitoring is
turned on for Sentinel.

69
00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.528
And the morning synchronization
probe gets its own custom table,

70
00:04:33.528 --> 00:04:36.093
written through the Logs Ingestion API.

71
00:04:36.093 --> 00:04:39.424
The check: a read-only
reachability test reports

72
00:04:39.424 --> 00:04:42.610
each table as delivering, late or missing.

73
00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:49.261
Step 2 fills one settings
file per environment,

74
00:04:49.261 --> 00:04:51.864
and checks the two values
the kit can't know:

75
00:04:51.864 --> 00:04:56.848
the compliance state your workspace records,
and the product names of D L P alerts.

76
00:04:56.848 --> 00:04:58.576
Those values, and every I D,

77
00:04:58.576 --> 00:05:03.185
go into the deployed workbook's
parameters, never into the template.

78
00:05:03.185 --> 00:05:07.254
Then the validator runs ten checks on
the template, which matters because

79
00:05:07.254 --> 00:05:11.923
Microsoft says an exported template embeds
sensitive values that should be masked.

80
00:05:11.923 --> 00:05:15.274
Step 3 plans the deployment
of one workbook resource

81
00:05:15.274 --> 00:05:18.473
and previews it with what-if,
which changes nothing.

82
00:05:18.473 --> 00:05:20.965
A second person approves the plan's hash,

83
00:05:20.965 --> 00:05:24.190
and the kit refuses any
plan that would delete.

84
00:05:27.940 --> 00:05:29.303
Step 4 deploys.

85
00:05:29.303 --> 00:05:33.660
Saving a shared workbook needs the
workbooks write permission, which Workbook

86
00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:36.037
Contributor grants, and deploying through

87
00:05:36.037 --> 00:05:38.678
Resource Manager also
needs deployment rights.

88
00:05:38.678 --> 00:05:42.977
Grant both on the workbook's resource
group only, for the deployment window.

89
00:05:42.977 --> 00:05:46.641
Readers need Workbook Reader and
their own access to the data.

90
00:05:46.641 --> 00:05:49.743
The test stage runs preflight,
plans with what-if,

91
00:05:49.743 --> 00:05:53.078
deploys the approved plan,
and checks reachability.

92
00:05:53.078 --> 00:05:56.203
It's a go when each of those
has a passing live record.

93
00:05:56.203 --> 00:05:58.339
Production runs the same commands,

94
00:05:58.339 --> 00:06:02.465
and the preflight refuses it until
the test stage's evidence passes.

95
00:06:02.465 --> 00:06:05.030
Rolling back deletes a view only.

96
00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:10.818
Step 5 is the morning read.

97
00:06:10.818 --> 00:06:13.306
Telemetry completeness comes first,

98
00:06:13.306 --> 00:06:17.080
because a dark source makes
every tab over it unreliable.

99
00:06:17.080 --> 00:06:21.337
Then each tab in turn: each
row that needs work becomes,

100
00:06:21.337 --> 00:06:24.142
or is matched to, a task with an owner.

101
00:06:24.142 --> 00:06:28.042
Entra Health and the I T S M
queue are worked where they live.

102
00:06:28.042 --> 00:06:33.029
The workbook never closes a task, pages
anyone, or proves a check happened.

103
00:06:33.029 --> 00:06:38.028
Step 6 keeps the evidence: the kit
records the validation, preflight, plan,

104
00:06:38.028 --> 00:06:43.192
deployment, reachability check and
rollback plan, each hashed and chained.

105
00:06:43.192 --> 00:06:45.467
A rendered view is never recorded.

106
00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:48.020
And a portal edit comes back as an export,

107
00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.940
is validated, and replaces
the template through review.

108
00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:59.555
The workbook supports the monitoring
the daily checks already do;

109
00:06:59.555 --> 00:07:00.890
it doesn't add a control.

110
00:07:00.890 --> 00:07:05.251
Its records support configuration and
change control for the template and the

111
00:07:05.251 --> 00:07:07.629
deployment, and continuous monitoring for

112
00:07:07.629 --> 00:07:10.140
the reachability check;
the assessor decides.

113
00:07:10.140 --> 00:07:13.133
The biggest dangers are a
dashboard taken as evidence,

114
00:07:13.133 --> 00:07:15.528
and a missing connector
that looks healthy.

115
00:07:15.528 --> 00:07:19.927
The guards are the banner, the refused
render, and stale shown as stale.

116
00:07:19.927 --> 00:07:23.187
Some things couldn't be
verified on Microsoft Learn:

117
00:07:23.187 --> 00:07:27.051
the workbook's item format field
by field, G C C for Entra Health

118
00:07:27.051 --> 00:07:30.916
and Connect Health, and the values
your own workspace records.

119
00:07:30.916 --> 00:07:34.230
The developer workbook and the
learning path take it from here.
